<title>UK: Copper concentrate ship unloading after inspection.</title>
<headline>Copper concentrate ship unloading after inspection.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Panama-flagged bulker Ypapadi was unloading its cargo at Gaspe, Canada after completing an inspection for potential damage following its recent grounding, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said.</p>
<p>The 30,330 dwt vessel, carrying 2,500 tonnes of copper concentrate, grounded on December 7 off Nova Scotia around Latitude 48 51N, Longtitude 64 25.2W.</p>
</text>
